<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ARTIFACT ONLY: a reviewable per-user LaunchAgent for the on-demand Quick
  Tunnel.

  NOT INSTALLED. Nothing in this repository installs, loads, bootstraps or
  kickstarts it. Installing it is a later, separately approved human step;
  see docs/tunnel.md, "The optional launchd job".

  DEFAULT OFF:
  - RunAtLoad is false and there is NO KeepAlive key, so loading this job
    starts nothing and launchd never restarts it.
  - It runs only when a human explicitly kickstarts it from a local shell.
  - It stops on `launchctl kill TERM` (or bootout), or on `ditunnel.py off`.

  THE JOB IS THE CONTROLLER: `ditunnel.py foreground` holds cloudflared as
  its own unreaped child (in cloudflared's own session) and stops it
  anchored.

  ExitTimeOut (420 s) is longer than the controller's worst-case bounded
  stop at the default stop grace, which is at most 343.05 s from the
  SIGTERM:
  - up to 1.05 s to observe the stop: 0.05 s at any wait (accept, receive,
    or reply piece; reads have one 2 s total deadline, and reads and status
    replies are abandoned on a pending stop), plus local work between waits,
    allowed 1 s as an assumption (not measured);
  - the first 20 s attempt (10 s SIGTERM grace, then two 5 s waits);
  - up to 1 s replying to a client's stop request;
  - a 300 s retry window, which includes the second attempt;
  - a final 1 s pause and 20 s attempt, begun just before that window
    closes.
  Record bookkeeping after the stop waits on the state lock, unbounded.
  - If the stop was observed, nothing is running, and a kill during that
    wait leaves only a record that a later off clears.
  - If the retries ran out, members may be alive, and a kill during that
    wait (or before the save) leaves survivors and a possibly stale
    "running" record. Recovery is then manual.
  This plist passes no stop-grace option. A larger grace needs a larger
  ExitTimeOut.

  The anchor is LOST if the retries run out with a member still alive (the
  record is kept as stop_unconfirmed), or if launchd kills the job before
  its stop completes. The tool then signals nothing; recovery is manual. See
  docs/tunnel.md, "Manual recovery".

  Every /ABSOLUTE/PATH and PORT placeholder must be replaced before
  installation. Left as is, the job refuses to start (PORT is not a number).

  Its label is deliberately distinct from any existing tunnel job.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.dodginginfinity.ditunnel</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/python3</string>
		<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/dodging-infinity/ditunnel.py</string>
		<string>--state-dir</string>
		<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/owner-only/ditunnel-state</string>
		<string>foreground</string>
		<string>--port</string>
		<string>PORT</string>
		<string>--cloudflared</string>
		<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/cloudflared</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<false/>
	<key>ExitTimeOut</key>
	<integer>420</integer>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/owner-only/ditunnel-state/launchd.out</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/owner-only/ditunnel-state/launchd.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
